<h2 id="faq-heading">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
<div class="usa-accordion usa-accordion--bordered usa-accordion--multiselectable" data-allow-multiple="">
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="faq-1">What is an infeed conveyor?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-1" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>Delivers products to a downstream machine at the precise speed, spacing, and orientation required. Uses timing screws, starwheels, servo phasing, or flights to convert random flow into timed machine-ready spacing.</p>

</div>
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-2">What is a timing screw?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-2" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>A helical screw rotating alongside a conveyor that captures round containers and spaces them at precise pitch. Dominant for bottles, cans, and jars before filling, labeling, and capping. Fixed screws need physical swapping; servo screws adjust electronically.</p>

</div>
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-3">What is a starwheel?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-3" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>A rotating disc with pockets matching the container diameter. Captures containers and delivers them at precise timing to rotary machines (fillers, cappers, labelers). Pocket count and speed synchronize with the machine cycle.</p>

</div>
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-4">What is a servo infeed?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-4" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>Servo-driven belts or flights that control product spacing for any product shape (not just round containers). Recipe-based pitch adjustment. Replaces fixed-pitch timing screws on multi-SKU lines. Flight conveyors achieve ±0.5-1.0mm accuracy.</p>

</div>
